<Project>
  <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\ProductVersion.props"
          Condition="Exists('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\ProductVersion.props')" />
  <!--
    Shared MSBuild properties for every project under modules/.

    WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: modules/ sat outside src/, and src/Directory.Build.props was the repo's
    ONLY one, so no module project inherited any of the shared settings. MSBuild walks UP from the
    project directory to find Directory.Build.props, and modules/AiBrain/ never reaches src/. Each
    module csproj had therefore been repeating (or quietly missing) what src/ sets once.

    The leak this closes, found 2026-09-10 by auditing what actually ships. Every DLL inside the six
    tracked modules-dist/*.zip carried a PE CodeView (RSDS) debug record naming the maintainer's
    absolute build path:

        D:\...\projects\desktop-ai-companion\modules\AiBrain\obj\Release\AiBrain.pdb

    Those zips are served to every user from master via raw.githubusercontent, so that string was
    published. No .pdb is shipped in the zip at all, the payload is the DLL, deps.json and the
    WinRT/SDK assemblies, so the record pointed at a file no user could ever have, and existed
    purely as machine metadata. src/DesktopAICompanion_Portable.csproj already sets DebugType=none
    for Release for the app; this makes the modules match, which is why the app was never affected.

    Deterministic + ContinuousIntegrationBuild alone do NOT fix it: ContinuousIntegrationBuild is
    gated on $(CI) in src/Directory.Build.props, and the module zips are produced LOCALLY by
    packaging/New-ModuleDistZip.ps1 where CI is unset. Suppressing the record is the fix that does
    not depend on who runs the build.

    Debug builds keep full symbols; only Release drops them, and only Release is ever published.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>7.3</LangVersion>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release'">
    <!-- No PDB, and therefore no absolute path embedded in the assembly. -->
    <DebugType>none</DebugType>
    <DebugSymbols>false</DebugSymbols>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
